{
  "_comment": [
    "British spelling -> American spelling, for ASD-STE100 rule 1.14.",
    "The standard states the rule but gives no word list, so this file is ours.",
    "Keys are lowercase. The linter matches whole words and keeps the original case.",
    "",
    "Only unambiguous pairs belong here. Words where the British form is also a",
    "correct American word with a different meaning are left out on purpose:",
    "  'programme' is safe, but 'program' is not a British-only spelling",
    "  'draught' is safe, but 'draft' means something else too",
    "  'metre'/'litre' are safe, but 'meter' is also an instrument"
